["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>About 2 weeks to go. Gear and practice take longer than you think. This is the order that works.</p></aside>","<ul><li><strong>Week 1 (now):</strong> licences, buy the shotgun, buy and mount the scope.</li><li><strong>Week 2:</strong> sight in the rifle, pattern the shotgun, buy clothing, scout on the map.</li><li><strong>Hunt week:</strong> final checks, pack, go.</li><li>Dates are a plan, not a rule. Move them to fit your life.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Licences and the scope come first. Without a sighted in rifle there is no deer hunt. Without a federal permit there is no duck hunt.</p></aside>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"cd-w1\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:0\"><span>Find my FWID (Fish and Wildlife ID) in WILD online</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:1\"><span>Buy BC hunting licence online</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:2\"><span>Buy mule deer and white tailed deer licences IN PERSON</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:3\"><span>Buy the federal Migratory Game Bird Hunting Permit online</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:4\"><span>Pick a shotgun (Session 3) and buy it</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:5\"><span>Buy steel shot for ducks and lead or steel for quail (Session 6)</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:6\"><span>Pick a scope and Picatinny rings (Session 4) and buy them</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:7\"><span>Have the shop mount the scope, or mount it with a torque wrench</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:8\"><span>Buy .308 ammo: 3 to 4 boxes of the SAME load</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w1:9\"><span>Ask your brother: is his own house on the 20 acres? Where are the neighbours?</span></label></div>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"cd-w2\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:0\"><span>Bore sight, then zero the rifle at 100 m (Session 5)</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:1\"><span>Shoot 3 shot groups from a rest until they are tight</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:2\"><span>Shoot from sitting and kneeling with shooting sticks</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:3\"><span>Pattern the shotgun on paper with your duck load (Session 5)</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:4\"><span>Practice on clay targets, at least 1 session</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:5\"><span>Buy clothing, boots, waders (Session 7)</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:6\"><span>Build the day pack and car kit (Session 8)</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:7\"><span>Download offline maps of the area to your phone</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:8\"><span>Scout on the map: slopes, benches, water, roads (Sessions 9 to 11)</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w2:9\"><span>Practice the legal to shoot flowchart in Field Mode</span></label></div>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"cd-w3\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w3:0\"><span>Check in season regulation changes at <a href=\"https://www.gov.bc.ca/huntingregulations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gov.bc.ca/huntingregulations</a>, and closures</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w3:1\"><span>Check fire restrictions and road closures</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w3:2\"><span>Check legal light times in Field Mode</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w3:3\"><span>Leave a trip plan with someone</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w3:4\"><span>Pack: licences, ID, permit, ammo, knife, game bags, first aid</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w3:5\"><span>Cooler and ice ready for meat</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"cd-w3:6\"><span>Go slow. Watch more than you walk.</span></label></div>","<ul><li>Buy where you can handle the gun and get help mounting the scope. (Tip)</li><li>Ask the store about a range near Kamloops. Many have sighting in days. (Tip)</li><li>One ammo load for the rifle. Do not mix brands after zeroing. (Tip, 85% the zero changes between loads)</li><li>Practice loading and unloading at the car until it is boring. (Tip)</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Buy once, practice twice. The rifle you shot 60 times beats the fancy one you shot 6 times.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Mounting the scope the night before the hunt.</li><li>Buying 5 kinds of ammo and never zeroing any of them.</li><li>Spending every evening shopping and none on the range.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Tonight: put your hunt date in More. Then tick off the first 3 boxes above.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Licence facts: see Session 2 sources (official synopsis pages 5 to 8, read directly 2026-10-02).</li><li>In season changes: the synopsis says to check <a href=\"https://www.gov.bc.ca/huntingregulations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gov.bc.ca/huntingregulations</a> before your hunt, page 7 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Checked 2026-10-02.</li><li>Everything else in this session is a plan and tips (opinion), not rules.</li></ul>"]